  {
   "type": "text",
   "tag": "declared",
   "text": "Reassemble the kernel tarball: cat linux/linux-4.15.tar.xz.part00 linux/linux-4.15.tar.xz.part01 linux/linux-4.15.tar.xz.part02 > linux-4.15.tar.xz && sha256sum linux-4.15.tar.xz  (expect 5a26478906d5005f4f809402e981518d2b8844949199f60c4b6e1f986ca2a769). Then: tar xf linux-4.15.tar.xz && cd linux-4.15 && git apply ../linux/riscv-linux-v4.15..a3b1e7acc6a1.patch (or patch -p1) && patch -p1 < ../bellard/riscv-linux.diff && cp ../bellard/config_linux_riscv64 .config && make ARCH=riscv olddefconfig vmlinux."
  },
  {
   "type": "text",
   "tag": "declared",
   "text": "WRITTEN OFFER (valid at least three years from 2026-10-11, to any third party, at no charge beyond the cost of physically performing distribution): The publisher of rizal.info / rizal.pw (Charles Augustus Marcum III, GitHub rizalward, https://github.com/rizalward/rizal.info/issues) will provide, on request, any further complete corresponding source we hold or obtain for: (1) the exact kernel .config and toolchain of build #11 (Nov 8 2018) — Fabrice Bellard published only config_linux_riscv64 of build #10 (Sep 2018, same a3b1e7a tree), included here; (2) the BusyBox 1.21.1 .config used for the rootfs; (3) the glibc 2.24.90 riscv snapshot source. These binaries are redistributed unmodified from Bellard's jslinux-2019-12-21 demo pack; the upstream author has not published items (1)-(3). Honest status: kernel and BusyBox version source = exact; build configs and glibc snapshot = written offer."
  },
